course: dictionary
lesson: 7194
title: Pesticides and the pests they kill
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pesticide is a chemical that kills pests. A pest is anything that damages crops or gardens, such as insects, weeds, fungi or small animals. The word is built from clues too: the ending -cide means killing, as in insecticide.
explain: Read the context: «Many bees have become fewer because of lost wild flowers, some pesticides, disease and changing weather.» Pesticides are on a list of things that harm bees, so they must be harmful to living creatures. Try your meaning in the sentence: "some chemicals used to kill pests" still makes sense there.
explain: «The bald eagle came back after the pesticide DDT, which made its eggshells thin, was banned.» Banned means stopped by law. The clue tells you DDT was harmful enough to be stopped, and the eagles recovered once it was.
fact: A pesticide is a chemical used to kill pests.
fact: Insecticides kill insects, herbicides kill weeds, and fungicides kill moulds and fungi.
fact: You may hear the phrases «spray pesticides» and «pesticide-free».
fact: Pesticides are poisonous, so keep them away from children and pets, and wash fruit before you eat it.
fact: Natural methods, such as ladybirds eating aphids, are an alternative to pesticides.
exercise: «Many bees have become fewer because of lost wild flowers, some pesticides, disease and changing weather.» What is a pesticide? | A wild flower that grows in fields | A kind of bee that lives in a hive | *A chemical used to kill pests | A type of weather
exercise: A herbicide is a kind of pesticide. What does a herbicide kill? | Small birds | Moulds and fungi | *Weeds | Insects
exercise: «The bald eagle came back after the pesticide DDT, which made its eggshells thin, was banned.» What does banned mean? | *Stopped by law | Painted bright red | Sold in shops | Flown to another country
test: Which pests does a fungicide kill? | Insects | Weeds | Wild flowers | *Moulds and fungi
test: Why should you wash fruit before you eat it? | *Pesticides are poisonous, so washing helps remove them | Washing stops fruit from growing | Fruit is always safe to eat raw | Pesticides make fruit sweeter
exam: Which is a natural way to deal with pests instead of pesticides? | *Ladybirds eating aphids | Leaving pesticides in rivers | Spraying every plant with fungicide | Keeping pesticides near children
